{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/783029-hurt-locker-explosives-mechanics","id":783029,"title":"Hurt Locker Explosives Mechanics","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-09T13:24:23-08:00","id":783029,"title":"Hurt Locker Explosives Mechanics","content":"I remember there being talk about these being re-written for the final product, can we get any hint at what was changed? I really want to use explosives in my game, but I am leery of doing so with 1e mechanic to back it up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T20:04:19-08:00","id":783211,"title":"","content":"I should have some more information for you very soon, in fact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T20:10:17-08:00","id":783213,"title":"","content":"Awesome, thanks Claire. <br /> <br /> I just wanna clarify, I like the stuff in the drafts, I'm really just curious if there are any better solutions that emerged from giving it another look.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-09T20:21:43-08:00","id":783214,"title":"","content":"Yeah, we're going for a more simplified expression. Ultimately, explosives damage doesn't need to be broken down in much more detail than regular weapon damage. It's (usually) far less common, and something you want to be able to do adjudicate relatively quickly. All the better for getting to &quot;My vampire/werewolf/shielded mage just tanked that shit. What's the look on that fucker's face <i>now</i>?&quot; or &quot;The blast wave shatters their bones in its heat and pressure, leaving only smoking bits of charred flesh as reminders of the people they once were\u2014people with dreams, families, and lives of their own.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T17:49:10-08:00","id":783797,"title":"","content":"Okay, so the current rules are similar to those in the draft, but I wanted something a bit simpler and quicker to resolve. This just covers the explosion itself, and not the throwing of grenades or the like. Also note that explosives damage can inflict Tilts, too, such as Knocked Down, Deafened, Stunned, Arm/Leg Wrack.<br /> <br /> Basically, explosives have a Damage rating and a Force rating. They also have 3 blast areas: ground zero, primary, and secondary. The type of damage they deal depends on where you are caught in the blast, with GZ generally being aggravated, primary blast area being lethal, and secondary blast area being bashing. The explosive's Damage rating represents the initial detonation. If you're caught in the blast area, you take that much damage automatically. Storytellers roll an explosive's Force rating as an attack dice pool, to which Defense does not apply (at least, without the use of magic). Mundane armor only counts as half its rating against explosive damage. If even one success is achieved on the Force roll, add the Damage rating in automatic successes as additional damage (like regular weapon attacks).<br /> <br /> For example, Joe McVictim is at ground zero of a grenade going off. He takes 2 aggravated damage automatically (its Damage rating). The Storyteller rolls Force 3 and achieves one success. The grenade's Damage is added as automatic damage as well, inflicting a total of 3 additional levels of damage. Thus, Joe McVictim suffers 5 aggravated damage, is likely to bleed out, and probably suffers a variety of Tilts, as well. If Joe McVictim was in the PBA, he would have taken 5 lethal instead, or 5 bashing in the secondary blast area, and would have been left with ringing ears and a lot of sore bruises.<br /> <br /> Supernatural beings tend to react differently. In general, undead like vampires only suffer bashing outside of ground zero, unless it's a real fiery explosion, like an incendiary grenade or something. Mages without shielding spells or some other magic to drain the force or otherwise change the explosion suffer damage as mortals do. I figure werewolves in Hishu and Urhan suffer damage like mortals do, but you could make a case for Gauru at least to weather explosions better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T18:36:22-08:00","id":783819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/783029-hurt-locker-explosives-mechanics?p=783797#post783797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I figure werewolves in Hishu and Urhan suffer damage like mortals do, but you could make a case for Gauru at least to weather explosions better.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Werewolf rules in the current book state on page, 94, rules for Regeneration under &quot;Aggravated Damage&quot;:<br /> <br /> &quot;Only silver and supernatural powers (including Gifts, mage spells, and vampiric Disciplines) can cause aggravated damage to Uratha directly. Any source of harm that would cause aggravated damage to a human, including massive bodily devastation, only causes lethal damage to Uratha.&quot;<br /> <br /> So a point blank explosion would only cause lethal damage, since that falls under &quot;massive bodily devastation&quot;. This is for the universal regeneration rules, not the form specific ones. Unless of course, you or another writer overrules that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 12-10-2015, 09:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T19:45:39-08:00","id":783868,"title":"","content":"Ahhh, okay, I was going to check that, but it looks like you got there first. Appreciated! So yeah. Werewolves can tank explosions pretty well\u2014not as well as vampires, who simply just don't have a worry about squishy parts, but pretty close. Vampires take lethal at ground zero and bashing otherwise, and I'd probably rule that shielded mages or similar creatures (armored changelings, etc.) only suffer lethal even at ground zero.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-10T19:57:07-08:00","id":783880,"title":"","content":"I'd argue werewolves tank it better... largely because in Gauru they just heal it back up for no cost. I mean, how much damage do the various explosives do these days? I still go by the armory rules for missiles.<br /> <br /> And, you know, HE or Phosphorus explosives probably should be classified as fire damage....<br /> <br /> But that's all semantics, I suppose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T06:53:01-08:00","id":784708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/783029-hurt-locker-explosives-mechanics?p=783868#post783868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ahhh, okay, I was going to check that, but it looks like you got there first. Appreciated! So yeah. Werewolves can tank explosions pretty well\u2014not as well as vampires, who simply just don't have a worry about squishy parts, but pretty close. Vampires take lethal at ground zero and bashing otherwise, and I'd probably rule that shielded mages or similar creatures (armored changelings, etc.) only suffer lethal even at ground zero.</div> </div> </div> </div>That means that the vampire rule that all non magic weapons damage does only bashing damage to them is overruled there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T07:02:51-08:00","id":784714,"title":"","content":"Vampires take lethal damage instead of aggravated when they suffer massive bodily harm. So getting thrown into a wood chipper, or getting hit by a really fast car, or being at ground zero of an explosive all make sense for that sort of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T07:51:32-08:00","id":784740,"title":"","content":"ah nice didnt see that one rule^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-15T22:45:20-07:00","id":1537465,"title":"","content":"This was really useful this forum really does cover everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27607-bloodyrelight","name":"BloodyRelight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27607_2.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}